z9x-0007: PIN mode is enforced on the server (pair-verify before any media request)

Ours (Z9xAirPlay), against FDH2/UxPlay master 3dbf7ce after z9x-0001..0006 (paths relative
to UxPlay/lib). Applied by jni/build_native.sh inside a copy of UxPlay/lib with
patch -p1 --fuzz=0.
UxPlay never checked that a connection had paired before it handled fp-setup, SETUP,
RECORD or /play: only Apple senders that honour the TXT "pw" flag were held back.
- pairing.c/h: pairing_session_pin_paired() (pair-setup-pin step 3 succeeded).
- raop_handlers.h: in PIN mode pair-verify checks check_register() for every client that
  did not pair-setup-pin on this connection (a plain /pair-setup skipped it before); the
  connection counts as verified once step 2 proves the accepted key.
- raop.c: with use_pin, only /info, OPTIONS, the pairing requests, /server-info and the
  local HLS proxy are served before that; anything else gets RTSP 470 / HTTP 403. An
  AirPlay (HTTP) connection is admitted when a verified RAOP connection from the same
  address exists.
